Z||000000||GT Bastard||01-30-2000||08:22 PM||||I know the Fiero Store sells some suspension upgrades, but they're pretty steep.  Anybody know of another place. ||||reg||14
Z||000001||Monkeyman||01-30-2000||08:37 PM||||JCWhitney sell some lowering/sport springs and sway bars.  I think the sway bars are Addco and the springs are Suspension Technologies.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||01-30-2000||09:15 PM||||can anybody vouch for the quality? Have you ordered anything from them Monkey?  That's basically what I'm looking for(springs.)<P><BR>ps-i hope you finally got the virus straightened out monkey!||||reg||1
Z||000003||2birds||01-30-2000||09:41 PM||||I have the whole Whitney setup in mine, plus the Energy Suspension poly bushings.  The springs are linear rate, and are pretty harsh.  I think the eibach springs are progressive rate, and would be worth the extra cash if I was doing it again.  The handling improvement is really noticable, and it's definitely "in the weeds" now.  I'll try to post a pic when I find a good one, if anybody's interested.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Spyder||01-30-2000||10:11 PM||||My springs and sway bars came from JC Whitney. They are ADDCO and Suspension Techniques.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/suspension.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||stimpy||01-30-2000||11:09 PM||||Well, I don't know about Eibachs beingany smoother of a ride. Fieroshop recently removed my dad's Eibachs and replaced them w stock springs.  There was absolutely ZERO suspension travel in the front and they were very stiff in rears. If I were to be going for a lowered look in the front, my first pick would be some BellTech dropped spindles, possibly using lower springs in rear. My prorities right now are more twoards cosmetic, but I would like to hook up a rear sway bar soon. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||01-31-2000||12:22 AM||||I bought the Fiero Store KYB system along with all the Urethane Bushings. Yes it is up there in price but the ride is nice. Stiff but not annoying on long trips. The springs are progressive and lower the car 1 inch. I have seen other kits for less that are comparable and I have driven a few different Fieros with different set-ups and I liked this set-up the best for all around/daily driving. The Koni race suspension is great for racing/hard driving but it gets to you on a long drive. If you can find a local Fiero club and test drive different suspensions then decide what you want. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||GT Bastard||01-31-2000||03:19 AM||||Coooool.... While searching, I found some good stuff at <A HREF="http://www.carparts.com" TARGET=_blank>www.carparts.com</A>  <BR>They had some really nice prices for suspension and other fiero stuff.||||reg||1
